      "origin": {
        "statusEn": "Most Likely Origin; Exact First Use Uncertain",
        "statusZh": "最可能的來源；確切首次用法不明",
        "history": [
          {
            "titleEn": "The Historical Background",
            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "The figurative expression turn the tables is recorded from the seventeenth century. An early, frequently cited use is associated with a sermon preached by Robert Sanderson in 1634 and published in 1635. Existing records establish that the expression was in use during that period, but they do not prove who first created it or exactly when it entered spoken English.",
            "zh": "turn the tables 的比喻用法在十七世紀已有記錄。 一個經常被引用的早期例子，來自 Robert Sanderson 在1634年講道、並於1635年出版的文本。 現有資料證明這個表達在當時已有人使用， 但不能證明是誰首先創造它，也不能確定它在甚麼時候開始在口語中出現。"
          },
          {
            "titleEn": "How the Meaning Developed",
            "titleZh": "意思如何演變",
            "en": "The gaming image naturally came to represent a reversal of positions. One player had the better position, but the balance changed and the other player gained the advantage. Speakers later extended the image to arguments, competitions, business situations and personal conflicts.",
            "zh": "遊戲中雙方位置逆轉的畫面，逐漸被用來表示一般情況中的優劣逆轉。 一名玩家原本處於較有利位置，但局勢其後改變，另一名玩家反而取得優勢。 後來，這個意象被延伸至爭論、競賽、商業情況及人際衝突。"
          }
        ],
        "memoryEn": "Think of two players changing positions: the side that was losing now has the advantage.",
        "memoryZh": "想像兩名玩家的優劣位置對調：原本落後的一方現在反而取得優勢。"
      },
