            "titleEn": "The Historical Background",
            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "The exact first use of have sticky fingers has not been firmly identified. However, the related adjective sticky-fingered appeared in American newspaper examples in 1855 and 1857 to describe people associated with stealing. These records show that the metaphor was already being used by the middle of the nineteenth century, but they do not prove who invented the expression or exactly when the modern noun phrase first appeared.",
            "zh": "have sticky fingers 的確切首次用法尚未能確認。 不過，相關形容詞 sticky-fingered 在1855年及 1857年的美國報章例子中已用來形容與偷竊有關的人。 這些記錄顯示，這個比喻在十九世紀中期已有人使用，但不能證明是誰創造了這個表達，也不能確定現代名詞短語最早在何時出現。"
