            "en": "The first person to use big fish figuratively is not known. A.Word.A.Day reports an earliest documented use in 1827, while an American Heritage idiom entry states that big fish had been slang for an important or influential person since the early 1800s. These records show that the expression existed in writing by that period; they do not necessarily identify its first spoken use.",
