            "en": "A related longer expression appeared in John Norris’s Practical Discourses in 1698: “turn the deaf Ear, and the blind Eye.” A source citing the Oxford English Dictionary identifies this as an early recorded occurrence. The shorter form turn a blind eye is documented in an 1823 letter by Martha Wilmot.",
