      "origin": {
        "statusEn": "Gradual Development; Exact First Use Unknown",
        "statusZh": "逐漸形成；確切首次用法不明",
        "history": [
          {
            "titleEn": "The Historical Background",
            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "The precise first use of the modern expression point the finger at someone has not been firmly established. However, an 1828 edition of Webster’s dictionary recorded the wording “point the finger of scorn at one”, showing that the image of pointing a finger was already associated with public shame or reproach. A similar figurative use also appeared in an 1866 issue of The Atlantic Monthly. These examples provide evidence of the older image, but they do not prove exactly when the present-day blame expression was created.",
            "zh": "現時仍未能確定 point the finger at someone 這個現代用法最早在何時出現。 不過，1828 年版的 Webster’s Dictionary 已記錄 “point the finger of scorn at one”，反映以手指指向某人的畫面，當"
          },
          {
            "titleEn": "How the Meaning Developed",
            "titleZh": "意思如何演變",
            "en": "Because physically pointing at someone singles that person out, the image gradually became a metaphor for selecting someone as the person to blame. Today, point the finger at somebody means to accuse or blame that person for something bad.",
            "zh": "由於以手指指向某人會令該人成為眾人注意的對象，這個畫面逐漸演變成一個比喻，表示把某人挑出來承受指責。 今天，point the finger at somebody 表示指責或歸咎某人。"
          }
        ],
        "memoryEn": "The finger singles out one person; the idiom singles out the person being blamed.",
        "memoryZh": "手指指向一個人；慣用語則把那個人定為受到指責的對象。"
      },
