            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "An established idiom reference dates the expression to the early 1500s, but this should not be treated as proof of its exact first spoken use. By 1868, Louisa May Alcott used the expression naturally in Little Women, showing that it was already established in literary English by that time. The Library of Congress records the first edition of Little Women in 1868, while the University of Washington text preserves Alcott’s use of the expression.",
