            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "Merriam-Webster records 1838 as the first known use of the idiomatic expression. A travel book published in 1838 also described the back seat of a Paris omnibus as the last seat to be occupied and the most difficult one to reach. That passage is literal rather than idiomatic, but it shows how a back seat could suggest a less desirable or prominent position.",
            "zh": "Merriam-Webster 把1838年列為目前所知這個慣用語的最早使用年份。 同年出版的一本旅遊著作亦把巴黎公共馬車的後座形容為最後才有人坐、而且最難到達的位置。 該段文字屬於字面用法，不能證明慣用語由此而來，但它顯示後座可以令人聯想到較不理想或較不顯眼的位置。"
