      "benefits": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "titleEn": "It compresses a longer explanation",
          "titleZh": "好處一",
          "en": "It compresses a longer explanation. Instead of saying that a result was extremely disappointing and difficult to accept, the speaker can express the same central idea through one memorable phrase.",
          "zh": "它能濃縮較長的解釋。 說話者毋須完整重複「這個結果令人非常失望，而且很難接受」，便可用一個固定表達傳達核心意思。",
          "examples": []
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "titleEn": "It expresses reluctant acceptance",
          "titleZh": "好處二",
          "en": "It expresses reluctant acceptance. The idiom shows that the speaker or affected person does not welcome the situation but recognises that it must be faced.",
          "zh": "它能表達無奈接受。 這個慣用語顯示當事人並不歡迎這個處境，卻明白自己必須面對它。",
          "examples": []
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "titleEn": "It communicates emotional weight",
          "titleZh": "好處三",
          "en": "It communicates emotional weight. It can convey disappointment, hurt pride, frustration or sadness more clearly than a neutral phrase such as an unfortunate result.",
          "zh": "它能表達事情的情感分量，比 an unfortunate result 這類中性說法更能顯示失望、自尊受挫、沮喪或難過。",
          "examples": []
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "titleEn": "It helps speakers show empathy",
          "titleZh": "好處四",
          "en": "It helps speakers show empathy. Saying that something is a bitter pill for another person to swallow acknowledges how difficult the experience may be for that person.",
          "zh": "它有助說話者表達同理心。 說某件事是對方 a bitter pill to swallow，能承認那段經歷對對方而言確實很難受。",
          "examples": []
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "titleEn": "It works with different time and certainty frames",
          "titleZh": "好處五",
          "en": "It works with different time and certainty frames. The expression can describe a past result, a present difficulty, a future consequence or a possible outcome. This idiom is useful only when the situation genuinely involves an unpleasant reality that must be accepted. It is not automatically better than plain English.",
          "zh": "它可以配合不同時間及確定程度，用來描述過去結果、現在困境、未來後果或可能出現的情況。 只有當語境真正涉及一項必須接受的不愉快現實時，這個慣用語才合適。 它並非在所有情況下都比直接表達更好。",
          "examples": []
        }
      ],
