          "titleZh": "幫助理解真實英語",
          "en": "Learners may encounter the expression in conversations, films, interviews, news features and personal writing. An idiom is not automatically better than a plain expression. Use a black sheep only when the idea of group disapproval or exclusion is important. Model Examples Model 1: Misconduct Aaron has repeatedly cheated his relatives, so the whole family is ashamed of him. Model 2: Unfair rejection Lily has done nothing wrong, but her relatives reject her because she refuses to join the family business.",
