      "origin": {
        "statusEn": "Gradual Development; Exact Origin Unknown",
        "statusZh": "逐漸形成；確切來源不明",
        "history": [
          {
            "titleEn": "The Historical Background",
            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "The exact first use of the complete noun phrase a shoulder to cry on has not been clearly identified. Historical evidence does show the related figurative wording cry on someone’s shoulder in the early 1930s. A digitised American newspaper from 1932 contains the line “They used to cry on your shoulder,” while an etymological reference dates the figurative expression to about 1935. These related examples help document the image, but they should not automatically be treated as the first use of the exact modern noun phrase.",
            "zh": "這個完整名詞短語的確切首次用法尚未能確認。 不過，歷史資料顯示，cry on someone’s shoulder 這個相關的比喻說法在二十世紀三十年代初已經出現。 這些記錄可以證明相關意象已經存在，但不能自動被視為現代完整短語的首次用法。"
          },
          {
            "titleEn": "How the Meaning Developed",
            "titleZh": "意思如何演變",
            "en": "The literal act of leaning on a trusted person while crying gradually came to represent emotional support more generally. Today, the listener does not need to be physically present, and the upset person does not need to cry.",
            "zh": "在哭泣時靠在可信任的人身上這個實際動作，逐漸引申為一般的情緒支援。 今天，提供安慰的人不一定需要在身旁，而難過的人也不一定真的流淚。"
          }
        ],
        "memoryEn": "A physical shoulder supports the head; a figurative shoulder supports the person emotionally.",
        "memoryZh": "真正的肩膀承托頭部；比喻中的「肩膀」則承托一個人的情緒。"
      },
