            "titleEn": "The Historical Background",
            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "Etymonline records literal and broader figurative uses connected with changing direction from the 1680s. Dictionary.com dates the more specific meaning of passing a critical point and beginning to recover to the first half of the nineteenth century. It connects that later sense with passing a corner in a race, particularly a final corner. The precise first speaker and exact event that created the recovery meaning have not been established.",
            "zh": "Etymonline 的資料顯示，與改變方向有關的字面及較廣泛比喻用法可追溯至十七世紀八十年代。 Dictionary.com 則把「渡過關鍵階段並開始復原」這個較具體意思追溯至十九世紀上半葉，並把它與比賽中繞過彎角的畫面連繫起來。 至於確切由誰及在甚麼事件中首先創造這個康復意思，現時仍未能確認。"
