        "history": [
          {
            "titleEn": "The Historical Background",
            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "By 1910, slipping on a banana skin was already being used as an obvious example of physical comedy. A Smithsonian history of banana humour also records the gag in Harold Lloyd’s 1917 silent film The Flirt, while the Library of Congress describes banana peels being used to arrange a comic accident in the 1927 Laurel and Hardy film The Battle of the Century.",
            "zh": "早在1910年，踏中香蕉皮滑倒已被視為一種明顯的肢體喜劇例子。 這個橋段其後亦常見於默片及喜劇電影。"
          },
          {
            "titleEn": "How the Meaning Developed",
            "titleZh": "意思如何演變",
            "en": "A small and easily avoided object can suddenly bring down somebody who appears confident. The image therefore became a natural metaphor for an unexpected, foolish mistake that causes embarrassment or damages a person’s success. The precise first figurative use has not been firmly identified.",
            "zh": "一件細小而且本可避開的物件，可以突然令一個看似充滿信心的人跌倒。 因此，這個畫面逐漸成為比喻，用來形容意外而愚蠢的錯誤，令人出醜或破壞原有成果。"
          }
        ],
        "memoryEn": "A tiny banana skin can bring down a confident walker; one tiny mistake can bring down a confident person or team.",
        "memoryZh": "一塊小小的香蕉皮可以令自信的行人跌倒；一個小小的錯誤也可以令自信的人或團隊失手。"
