            "titleEn": "The Historical Background",
            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "The exact origin has not been proved. A widely cited early written example appeared in a 1952 review in The Economic Journal. The writer compared a reader repeatedly losing progress with being returned to square one in a game of snakes and ladders. This is strong early evidence of a board-game association, but it does not prove that one particular game created the expression. 證實。一個經常被引用的早期書面例子出現在1952年的《經濟學期刊》書評中。作者 把讀者反覆失去進展的情況,比作在蛇梯棋中被送回第一格。這是表達與棋盤遊戲有關的有力早 期證據,但不能證明它一定由某一種遊戲創造。",
