            "en": "The expression developed in the United States as cars became increasingly common in the early twentieth century. Historical researchers have located clear negative motoring uses by the mid-1910s and a broad figurative use in 1921. Etymonline records the expression by 1923, while some modern dictionaries give the broader period 1925–30. These different dates concern the earliest examples located by different researchers; none proves the exact moment when people first began saying the expression.",
