            "titleZh": "意思如何演變",
            "en": "The adjective running can mean lasting a long time or continuing without stopping. Oxford and Merriam-Webster both use a running battle as an example of this continuous meaning. The physical idea of a battle moving from place to place therefore developed naturally into the figurative idea of one disagreement returning on different occasions.",
