      "benefits": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "titleEn": "It Shows a High Degree of Conflict",
          "titleZh": "表示高度激烈的衝突",
          "en": "The second version shows a much more serious and sustained conflict.",
          "zh": "第二個版本顯示衝突更加嚴重，而且持續一段時間。",
          "examples": []
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "titleEn": "It Presents Both Sides as Fully Engaged",
          "titleZh": "顯示雙方都全力投入",
          "en": "The expression does not merely say that one side complained. It suggests that opposing sides are actively resisting each other.",
          "zh": "這個表達不只是說其中一方提出投訴，而是表示對立雙方都在積極抗衡。",
          "examples": []
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "titleEn": "It Can Describe Different Kinds of Struggle",
          "titleZh": "可以描述不同類型的鬥爭",
          "en": "a political dispute; a business competition; a legal case; a school disagreement; a struggle for control; a debate over rules; a sports contest.",
          "zh": "它可以自然地形容政治爭議、商業競爭、法律案件、校園爭議、控制權爭奪、規則辯論及體育競賽。",
          "examples": []
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "titleEn": "It Works in Several Sentence Positions",
          "titleZh": "可以置於多個句子位置",
          "en": "This flexibility helps learners create varied and natural sentences.",
          "zh": "這種靈活性有助學生寫出更多樣化和自然的句子。",
          "examples": []
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "titleEn": "It Can Express Possibility or Prevention",
          "titleZh": "可以表達可能性或避免衝突",
          "en": "The expression is therefore useful for describing not only existing conflict, but also predicted or avoided conflict.",
          "zh": "因此，這個表達不但可以描述已出現的衝突，也可以描述預計會出現或成功避免的衝突。",
          "examples": []
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "titleEn": "It Provides a Strong Journalistic Description",
          "titleZh": "提供有力的新聞式描述",
          "en": "Instead of repeatedly writing very fierce argument or very difficult competition, a writer can sometimes use a pitched battle when the intensity is genuinely supported. However, the expression is not automatically better than plain language. It should be used only when the conflict is serious enough.",
          "zh": "作者不必反覆使用 very fierce argument 或 very difficult competition； 如果語境確實足夠強烈，可以使用 a pitched battle。 不過，這個表達並不一定比普通說法更好。 只有當衝突確實足夠嚴重時才應使用。",
          "examples": []
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "statusEn": "Well Documented; Exact First Spoken Use Unknown",
        "statusZh": "有較充分記錄；確切首次口語用法不明",
        "history": [
          {
            "titleEn": "The Historical Background",
            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "Merriam-Webster dates the earliest known use of pitched battle to around 1616. Etymonline connects the phrase with the late-fifteenth-century sense of pitch meaning to fix or arrange forces in order. An earliest known written example does not necessarily identify the first person who ever spoke the phrase.",
            "zh": "Merriam-Webster 把目前已知最早的 pitched battle 用法追溯至約1616年。 Etymonline 則把這個短語連繫至十五世紀後期 pitch 表示固定或排列軍隊的意思。 現存最早書面例子並不一定代表第一位說出這個短語的人。"
          },
          {
            "titleEn": "How the Meaning Developed",
            "titleZh": "意思如何演變",
            "en": "Because both armies were prepared and directly committed to the confrontation, the expression came to suggest an intense struggle in which opposing sides were fully engaged. It was later extended beyond military contexts to disputes, competitions and arguments.",
            "zh": "由於雙方軍隊都已準備好並正面投入戰鬥，這個表達逐漸帶有「雙方全力投入的激烈鬥爭」之意， 後來再延伸至軍事以外的爭議、競爭和辯論。"
          }
        ],
        "memoryEn": "Both sides have taken their positions and are fully prepared to fight; neither side is giving way easily.",
        "memoryZh": "雙方都已站穩陣地並準備正面交鋒，誰也不願輕易讓步。"
      },
