        "history": [
          {
            "titleEn": "The Historical Background",
            "titleZh": "歷史背景",
            "en": "English in the early twentieth century. Early examples found by Merriam-Webster used it in sport to mean spoiling or upsetting an expected result. By 1911, it was being used in a context much closer to revealing information.",
            "zh": "為何成為這個表達的一部分，確切原因仍然不明。 一個流行說法把它與古希臘使用不同顏色豆子投票的方式連繫起來，但可靠語言證據並未證實這個解釋。 這個表達在二十世紀初的美式英語中出現。 早期例子曾在體育語境中表示破壞原有結果； 到了 1911 年，其用法已較接近今天的 「透露消息」。"
          },
          {
            "titleEn": "How the Meaning Developed",
            "titleZh": "意思如何演變",
            "en": "The older idea of upsetting or spoiling a situation gradually became connected with revealing information that changed or ruined a plan. At the same time, spill had long been capable of meaning letting information out. Together, these ideas produced the modern meaning of revealing a secret, often too early or carelessly.",
            "zh": "較早期的「破壞局面」意思，逐漸與透露消息、令原有計劃受到影響或破壞連繫起來。 同時，spill 早已有「把消息說出來」的比喻用法。 這些意思最終形成今天的「洩露秘密」，而且往往帶有過早公開或不小心的語氣。"
          }
        ],
        "memoryEn": "When the beans fall out, they cannot easily be hidden again. When a secret is revealed, it cannot easily become secret again.",
        "memoryZh": "豆子倒出來後，很難重新藏起來；秘密說出來後，也很難再次變回秘密。"
