            "en": "The verb dice has long meant playing games with dice and, by extension, taking a chance. Merriam-Webster records both senses and uses dice with death as an example of taking a chance. Historical word references trace the gaming sense of the verb to Middle English. However, the consulted authoritative dictionaries do not identify one proven inventor or one exact first use of the complete idiom.",
